Subject: src: on OpenVMS, run m4 without fork() and find m4 and the data files

bison runs m4 through create_pipe_bidi(), which needs fork(); OpenVMS has
none.  But bison writes all of m4's input before reading any of its
output, so on VMS files do the work of the two pipes: the muscles go to a
temporary file in SYS that is m4's standard input, m4's standard
output goes to another, and bison scans that once m4 has exited.

m4 runs in a subprocess (LIB, vms_spawn_image(), also used by
print-xml.c) executing a small generated DCL procedure that drops the
SYS and SYS it inherits and points its SYS/SYS
at the temporary files.  A vfork()/execv() child (vms1) inherited a
SYS redirected to a file and opened it again, leaving a new, empty
version of the user's file.  The arguments are quoted, so DCL keeps their
case ("-I"); m4's messages go to a temporary log copied to stderr.

The defaults for the M4 and BISON_PKGDATADIR environment variables are
the kits' locations: M4$ROOT:[BIN]M4.EXE (github.com/issinoho/vms-m4) and
/BISON$ROOT/data (BISON$ROOT:[DATA], in Unix style because bison appends
"/skeletons/..." to it).

